{# The banner at the top of a teacher's public page (design/validated/cours-en-ligne.md, §5): the
   title the teacher chose, centred, in the colour they chose, over their background colour and,
   when there is one, their picture. The teacher's name is written nowhere else on the page - it is
   theirs to put in the title.

   Shared, through {% embed %}, by the public page and by the preview of « Ma page », so the teacher
   sees the banner a visitor will. Both colours are `#rrggbb` and the height a number by
   construction (App\Entity\OnlineCoursePage) - and checked again here, since the preview may be
   drawn from a submission the form has just refused: nothing else reaches the style attribute.

   The height is the teacher's too, in pixels, a quarter less on a phone (app.css).

   Variables: banner_title, title_color, banner_color, banner_height, image_key (nullable); the `bar` block holds
   what sits in the top right corner. #}
{% set title_color = title_color matches '/^#[0-9a-fA-F]{6}$/' ? title_color : '#ffffff' %}
{% set banner_color = banner_color matches '/^#[0-9a-fA-F]{6}$/' ? banner_color : '#12344d' %}
{% set banner_height = banner_height matches '/^[0-9]{1,4}$/' ? banner_height : 230 %}
<header class="cm-pub-banner {{ image_key ? 'has-image' }}" style="--cm-pub-banner-bg: {{ banner_color }}; --cm-pub-banner-ink: {{ title_color }}; --cm-pub-banner-height: {{ banner_height }}px;">
    {% if image_key %}
        {# Decorative: the title says what the page is. #}
        <img class="cm-pub-banner__image" src="{{ file_url(image_key) }}" alt="">
    {% endif %}
    {% block bar %}{% endblock %}
    <h1 class="cm-pub-banner__title">{{ banner_title }}</h1>
</header>
